# DRIVE Workflow Rules

- Start each task by reading the relevant docs in `docs/`. If code will be changed, read the product, scope, architecture, reward, and roadmap docs first.
- Plan first, then implement. For non-trivial tasks, share the plan before editing.
- Do not add unrequested features, dependencies, app setup, screens, Firebase code, or integrations.
- Do not change unrelated files. Preserve user work and keep diffs narrow.
- Follow the roadmap in `docs/07-build-roadmap.md` unless the user explicitly changes priority.
- Once the app exists, run typecheck and lint after substantive implementation work. If either cannot run, explain why.
- After every task, provide a concise summary of changed files.
- After every task, explain how the change supports the DRIVE brief.
- If the user asks for something outside MVP scope, pause and ask for confirmation before building it.
